<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish Armada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1588">1588</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Armada · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-spanish-war-1585-1604">Anglo-Spanish War (1585–1604)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Spanish Armada was the fleet sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a> in 1588 to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. It was defeated by the English navy and storms around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-isles">British Isles</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> treat the failure as a symbol of the limits of Spanish power, though <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> remained a great power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-armada.jpg" alt="Spanish Armada" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robert Adams, Augustine Ryther · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armadaroute.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
